SONARQUBE - code quality Analysis
++++++Installation commands+++++
#! /bin/bash
#Launch an instance with 9000 and t2.medium
cd /opt/
wget https://binaries.sonarsource.com/Distribution/sonarqube/sonarqube-26.9.0.129388.zip
unzip sonarqube-26.9.0.129388.zip
yum install java-17-amazon-corretto -y
useradd sonar
chown sonar:sonar sonarqube-8.9.6.50800 -R
chmod 777 sonarqube-26.9.0.129388 -R
su - sonar

#run this on server manually
#sh /opt/sonarqube-26.9.0.129388/bin/linux/sonar.sh start
#echo "user=admin & password=admin"
launch instance > install sonar(wget+unzip+java-17version)> add user (for sonar access) > change owner and permissions to unzipped sonarqube file> cd to unzipped file & bin & Linux os> start sonar (./sonar.sh start) >Plugin SonarQube scanner install on Jenkins to integrate with SonarQube > Goto managejenkins/System/ > search for SonarQube installation > add name (Name is used in Jenkins pipeline steps) + sonar Server url (http://ipv4:9000) +add secret key as password(get PAT token from sonar project security and generate) > Add CQA stage on Pipeline >steps select pipeline syntax - search for (withsonar)> shell script fpr sonar analysis can get on sonar dashboard - Run analysis on your report section - select build tool then sh script will get> paste "sh ----" on steps inside withSonarQQubeEnv( name given on jenkins integration){ <here> } > check indentation on pipeline and then save > BUILD pipeline///
